From 55cea1ee757baef890d3fe0584cf1bf563927b24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:50:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] sim, coding: rand48 with explicit state, sys/syscall.h not
 syscall.h

Two glibc-only spellings that no other libc has:

  taus.c:31:23: error: variable has incomplete type 'struct drand48_data'
  taus.c:40:5: error: call to undeclared function 'srand48_r'
  nrLDPC_coding_segment_decoder.c:20:10: fatal error: 'syscall.h' file not found

set_taus_seed() used the glibc reentrant srand48_r() and mrand48_r() so
that seeding the Tausworthe generator does not disturb the process-wide
rand48 state. POSIX jrand48() takes the 48-bit state explicitly and
returns the same values when the state is seeded the way srand48() does
(0x330E in the low word, the 32-bit seed above it), so every seed gives
the same sequence as before on glibc as well.

<syscall.h> is the glibc shortcut for <sys/syscall.h>; the eleven files
that include it get the portable name.
